  "configuration_id": "config_013",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only models (especially scvi_n200 + multiprofile + avgpool at 0.650) dominate, while the only image test (resnet50, singleprofile) scored just 0.208, suggesting image features may be uninformative. However, this single data point conflates modality value with encoder quality. Uncertainty: We cannot yet tell whether images are fundamentally uninformative for this task or whether resnet50 is simply a poor image encoder for cellular profiles. This experiment tests imagenet_vit_l (a much stronger, pretrained vision transformer) in the simplest possible image-only setting, isolating the image encoder quality question without confounding effects from fusion, aggregation, or profile settings. Why this is the best next step: Before investing limited budget in any of the 36 multimodal configurations, we must resolve whether the image modality can contribute meaningful signal at all. If ViT-L also yields low accuracy, we can confidently rule out image/multimodal directions and focus remaining experiments on RNA-only refinements. If ViT-L performs substantially better, multimodal fusion becomes a high-value exploration target. This single experiment gates an entire branch of the search space and is therefore the highest-information-per-experiment choice."
}

